Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ============================================================================
; Strong-Name Verification Skip for Aras Innovator IOM Assemblies
; ============================================================================
;
; Aras.IOM.dll is strong-name signed by Aras with PublicKeyToken e33b67d3bb5581e4.
; It requires ALL its dependencies (Nito.AsyncEx.*, Aras.Cryptography, Aras.Net)
; to also be signed with the SAME key. However, the NuGet versions of these
; dependencies are unsigned, causing FileLoadException at runtime:
;
;   "A strongly-named assembly is required. (0x80131044)"
;
; This .reg file registers a strong-name verification skip for the specific
; Aras key token. After applying, the CLR will skip SN verification for all
; assemblies signed with this key, allowing unsigned dependencies to load.
;
; To apply:
;   1. Right-click this file → "Merge" (or double-click)
;   2. Click "Yes" when prompted by UAC (requires Administrator privileges)
;   3. Restart Inventor
;
; This is a ONE-TIME setup per machine. Once applied, all users on this
; machine benefit. No reboot required.
;
; For /? syntax: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\StrongName\Verification
; ============================================================================

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\StrongName\Verification\*,e33b67d3bb5581e4]
